  'Application for Vehicle Registration (Ministry of Transportation). Section 1 is the vehicle''s registrant: the owner''s corporation under a Lease (its RIN when on record; a new corporation''s RIN, issued on ON00453 at the same visit, is written in at the counter), the owner under Co-Registrant, the lessor (leased car) or CarmaCars (owned car) under a Transfer. Section 7 carries the VIN. Section 8 is signed by the registrant''s signer: the owner (or their corporation''s signing officer) under a Lease or Co-Registrant; CarmaCars'' signing officer under a Transfer, of a leased car too. To tick at the counter: "Number plates owned by other than above" when CarmaCars holds the plates as lessee (a Lease, a Transfer of a leased car), "Vehicle to be registered to 2 individuals" under Co-Registrant, "Attach plates on record" in section 2 and "fit" in section 3. Left blank on purpose: sex (the registry asks it of new individual plate registrants only), the new plates question (the plate on record is attached), section 7''s insurer and policy (the fleet policy is written at the counter), the date of the signature and the office-use page. The lessor''s RIN and address under a Transfer of a leased car are on the lease and written at the counter. Only the empty text boxes are filled; the publisher''s PDF is otherwise unchanged. Checkboxes and drop-downs are left for the person at the counter, and every signature and its date are written in ink there. Mapping checked against the official PDF (https://forms.mgcs.gov.on.ca/dataset/3c75269a-0400-4861-baf2-93a5d668f57c/resource/339a68c4-afe9-4cc8-a372-7c1665e27d14/download/sr-lv-006e.pdf, SHA-256 df4831f0bdcfc794a901f6dff79423e6982980276a3dc659edeed68162c9cc49); check it with a preview before use.');
