  'Sworn Statement for the Transfer of a Used Vehicle (Ministry of Finance, retail sales tax): the recipient (the owner''s corporation) and the donor (the owner) swear the transfer is tax exempt. It is sworn before a commissioner, so it is printed and signed in person; the form has no signature fields. Left blank on purpose: the City or Town words and the county or regional municipality boxes (they depend on the municipality), the acquisition date and the reasons (the owner writes them), and the commissioner block (sworn in person). Only the empty text boxes are filled; the publisher''s PDF is otherwise unchanged. Checkboxes and drop-downs are left for the person at the counter, and every signature and its date are written in ink there. Mapping checked against the official PDF (https://forms.mgcs.gov.on.ca/dataset/64812fe6-775c-4fbd-98c9-bc9a1c6b1a38/resource/f165f763-c47f-4024-9b16-da60f741e79e/download/1155e.pdf, SHA-256 a2f38dc0ca7ea9b3b9c2369af7b21d6b4694241f1d5eb42b889559246166eb5b); check it with a preview before use.');
